<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd" identifier="pcb-item-45c638a43908404cb65a5084a5899f26" title="sat-c3-u01-lingering.html qc1" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>C</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float"><qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value></qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses &quot;lingering&quot; correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">The sprinter&apos;s lingering start won the race, exploding off the blocks faster than anyone else in the field.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">The bakery&apos;s lingering grand opening drew a line around the block on its very first morning of business.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">Weeks after the argument, a lingering coolness between the roommates showed in short answers and closed doors.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">He gave the piano a lingering polish in under a minute, one hurried wipe before the first guests arrived.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Lingering means lasting longer than expected and slow to fade or leave, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because an explosive start off the blocks is the fastest thing in the sentence — nothing about it stays or fades slowly.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Lingering means lasting longer than expected and slow to fade or leave, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because a grand opening on its very first morning is just beginning — the word watches things end, not launch.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Lingering means lasting longer than expected and slow to fade or leave, so it&apos;s the correct answer because the coolness between the roommates is still hanging on weeks after the argument, showing itself in small ways instead of clearing.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Lingering means lasting longer than expected and slow to fade or leave, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because one hurried wipe in under a minute is the opposite of taking your time — nothing here is drawn out.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
